; A document CONDUCTED by a file that is not beside it — the one anchor
; whose absence is not a detail.
;
; Plan 03: the anchor keeps time for a conducted document. So with no
; readable file there is no tempo map to read, and plan 03's placeholder
; (500 000 microseconds per quarter note in [4 4]) is all any position
; can be answered with. That used to be SILENT for a by-reference anchor
; — `validate` said nothing, `timeline` printed the placeholder and
; `export-score` wrote `:bpm 120` under a header naming the conductor —
; which is the final review's C1.
;
; Now it is an error at the anchor's span, twice over: the resolver's own
; `anchor_unavailable` (the file could not be read) and the conductor's
; (so every position is the placeholder's). `export-score` refuses on it
; and writes nothing at all, because a score is its transport.
;
; Compare `missing-anchor.sjon`, whose timeline is native: an anchor that
; merely carries CONTENT is recorded unresolved and the document is still
; a document.
(timeline :length 1bar :conductor song)

(anchor :id song :kind smf :file "absent.mid" :size 76 :sha256 "f2964bb1df2139ef13cbae50f323f2aacdfa7aed09b2dc001765db72baf48d6e")
